491:     #  ==== THE STORE SIDE OF THE ADDRESSING-MODE PRODUCT ====
492:     #
493:     #  *** THESE CELLS HAD NO ROW AT ALL, and the gap was invisible because `p`
494:     #  and `u` are ONE SELECTOR, not two bits: together they name the ADDRESSING
495:     #  MODE.  The code tests them NESTED (`if (p_bit) { if (u_bit)`), the
496:     #  architecture names the pair as one field, and generate_arm_multi.c:120
497:     #  switches on `p*2+u`.  Every store row here was STM**IA**, and Thumb PUSH
498:     #  is hardcoded **DB** (cpu_arm.c:1670) -- so IB and DA were never driven on
499:     #  the store side at any residue or strength.  A round block claiming *"Thumb
500:     #  PUSH already varies p and u there"* was two modes of four stated as an
501:     #  axis: the dropped-qualifier class. ***
502:     #
503:     #  EVERY ROW BELOW SITS AT AN ACCESS ADDRESS = 7 (mod 8).  THAT IS THE
504:     #  GEOMETRIC FIX FOR THE WHOLE CHAIN: 0x21007 has bits 0, 1 AND 2 set, so
505:     #  ~1, ~2, ~3 and ~7 are ALL discriminated by ONE access.  Every earlier
506:     #  repair placed its rows at the residue of the mutant it had just found
507:     #  (2 for ~1, bit-2-set for ~7) -- which is precisely why each pass found
508:     #  the next strength.  0x21007 & ~3 == 0x21004, so the word must land at
509:     #  PAGE_STM+4 and PAGE_STM must stay ZERO; both halves are asserted so the
510:     #  row cannot pass by the value merely being absent from one place.
